## Question 4: Fit the PCA using `prcomp`

Fit a PCA using `prcomp()`. Centre the variables and apply the scaling decision made in Question 3.

Store the fitted object as `mali_pca_fit`.

```{r}
#| label: fit-mali-pca


mali_pca_fit=prcomp(
  ~ .,
  data = mali_pca_clean,
  retx = TRUE,
  scale.=TRUE # scale since the feature magnitudes/variances are not comprable
)



```

The main parts of the fitted object are:

-   `mali_pca_fit$rotation`: the loading vectors;
-   `mali_pca_fit$x`: the principal component scores; and
-   `mali_pca_fit$sdev^2`: the variance of each principal component.

Confirm that the score matrix has one row per observation and one column per principal component.

```{r}
#| label: inspect-mali-pca-object


dim(mali_pca_fit$x) # PCA scores of every observation

dim(mali_pca_clean) # object dimensions equals the simensions of the original data

summary(mali_pca_fit)

data.frame(mali_pca_fit$rotation)
```

## Question 5: Fit the PCA using `eigen`

Fit the PCA using the eigen decomposition of the covariance/correlation matrix (depending on the decision you made earlier regarding standardisation). Confirm that the results are equivalent to those from `prcomp()`.

```{r}

# using eignen on the correlation matrix, since we decided to standardize the data

cor_matrix <- mali_pca_clean %>%
  select(where(is.numeric)) %>%
  cor(use = "complete.obs")

cor_matrix=as.matrix(cor_matrix)

#REMEBER, EIGENVALS -VARIANCES OF THE PCs
eigen(cor_matrix)$values; # THE SAME, YAY!
mali_pca_fit$sdev^2

# CHECK EIGENVECTORS= LOADING VECTORS/WEIGHT VECTORS

eigen(cor_matrix)$vectors; # THE SAME, YAY!
mali_pca_fit$rotation

```

## Question 6: Examine the variation explained

Calculate the proportion and cumulative proportion of variation explained by each principal component. Use both the output from `prcomp` and the eigen decomposition to confirm that the results are equivalent.

Store the results in a table called `mali_pve_tbl`.

```{r}
#| label: calculate-mali-pve

# CALL summary on prcomp to get the cumulative and proportion of variance explained
summary(mali_pca_fit)

# Using eignevals
eigen(cor_matrix)$values
var_prop=eigen(cor_matrix)$values/sum(eigen(cor_matrix)$values);var_prop

cum_var=c()
for (i in length(var_prop)){
  cum_i=sum(var_prop[1:i])/sum(var_prop)
  cum_var=c(cum_var,cum_i)
}

cum_var # THE SAME YAY!

mali_pve_tbl=summary(mali_pca_fit)
```

